      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9156-1",
        "name": "USN-9156-1",
        "description": "Albert Yang and Quang Luong discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly handle certain inputs. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-114938)  It was discovered that the JGSS component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114939)  Nicholas Carlini discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114940)  It was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114941)  It was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114942)  It was discovered that the Hotspot component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114943)  Alexander Dezhinov, Stanislav Dukhin, Nikita Kozlov, and Binbin Xu discovered that the Core Java Libraries component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114944)  It was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114945)  It was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 21 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114946)  Please see the following for more information: https://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-11-17",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-114938",
          "CVE-2026-114939",
          "CVE-2026-114940",
          "CVE-2026-114941",
          "CVE-2026-114942",
          "CVE-2026-114943",
          "CVE-2026-114944",
          "CVE-2026-114945",
          "CVE-2026-114946"
        ]
